24. Senior Management shall be responsible for ensuring that there are
adequate policies and procedures for carrying out the significant
activities of the institution on both long-term and day-to-day basis. This
responsibility includes ensuring that there are:

a) clear lines of responsibility for managing risk;
b) adequate systems for measuring risk;
c) appropriately planned limits on risk-taking;
d) effective internal controls; and
e) comprehensive risk-reporting process.
